{
    "title": "Ballistics Calculator 2024",
    "description": "This ballistics trajectory calculator app will help you always hit the target.\r\n\r\nFeatures:\r\n\r\n- Ammunition: 3000 cartridges in the database \r\n- 3000 reticles in the database\r\n- Graphic display of the trajectory\r\n- A visual comparison of the trajectories of different cartridges\r\n- Visualization of reticles, distance corrections (rifle scope calculator)\r\n- Different Ballistics Coefficients (G1,G7..)\r\n- Barometric pressure\r\n- Altitude\r\n- Temperature\r\n- Wind direction\r\n- Wind speed\r\n- Imperial and metric units\r\n- light ballistic calculator, very easy to use\r\n- Create your own rifle and custom ammo\r\n\r\nThe most accurate method of calculation. With this long range ballistics  calculator you can calculate range, bullet flight time, velocity, line of sight drop, wind drift, energy and see the visualization of the calculation on the reticle or on the chart. \r\n\r\nThe ballistic calculator allows you to use different units of measurement: MOA or mil (MRAD), inches or centimeters, yards or meters and so on.\r\n\r\nBullet velocity balistic calculator allows to use your own custom ammo or select ammunition from cartridge database. Database of the ballistics calculator app includes muzzle velocity, bullet weight, ballistic coefficient and other data for more than 3000 cartridges.",
    "descriptionHTML": "This ballistics trajectory calculator app will help you always hit the target.<br><br>Features:<br><br>- Ammunition: 3000 cartridges in the database <br>- 3000 reticles in the database<br>- Graphic display of the trajectory<br>- A visual comparison of the trajectories of different cartridges<br>- Visualization of reticles, distance corrections (rifle scope calculator)<br>- Different Ballistics Coefficients (G1,G7..)<br>- Barometric pressure<br>- Altitude<br>- Temperature<br>- Wind direction<br>- Wind speed<br>- Imperial and metric units<br>- light ballistic calculator, very easy to use<br>- Create your own rifle and custom ammo<br><br>The most accurate method of calculation. With this long range ballistics  calculator you can calculate range, bullet flight time, velocity, line of sight drop, wind drift, energy and see the visualization of the calculation on the reticle or on the chart. <br><br>The ballistic calculator allows you to use different units of measurement: MOA or mil (MRAD), inches or centimeters, yards or meters and so on.<br><br>Bullet velocity balistic calculator allows to use your own custom ammo or select ammunition from cartridge database. Database of the ballistics calculator app includes muzzle velocity, bullet weight, ballistic coefficient and other data for more than 3000 cartridges.",
